From: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: net: wireless: Add the Seekwave SV6160 Lite loader

The SV6160 Lite (SWT6621S) loads its firmware over SDIO under a
reset line, which the MMC power sequence also drives, and signals with
a pair of wake lines, one each way. Describe the three GPIOs.

Signed-off-by: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
---
 .../bindings/net/wireless/seekwave,sv6160lite.yaml        | 36 ++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 36 insertions(+)

--- /dev/null
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/net/wireless/seekwave,sv6160lite.yaml
@@ -0,0 +1,36 @@
+# SPDX-License-Identifier: (GPL-2.0-only OR BSD-2-Clause)
+%YAML 1.2
+---
+$id: http://devicetree.org/schemas/net/wireless/seekwave,sv6160lite.yaml#
+$schema: http://devicetree.org/meta-schemas/core.yaml#
+
+title: Seekwave SV6160 Lite SDIO firmware loader
+
+maintainers:
+  - Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
+
+description: |
+  Platform control for the Seekwave SDIO transport and firmware loader.
+  The reset line is also consumed by the MMC power-sequence provider.
+
+properties:
+  compatible:
+    const: seekwave,sv6160lite
+
+  reset-gpios:
+    maxItems: 1
+    description: Active-low radio reset shared with MMC power sequencing.
+
+  host-wake-gpios:
+    maxItems: 1
+    description: Wake indication from the radio.
+
+  chip-wake-gpios:
+    maxItems: 1
+    description: Wake request to the radio.
+
+required:
+  - compatible
+  - reset-gpios
+
+additionalProperties: false
